              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: The authException.getMessage() string, which can contain user-controlled input (e.g., failed credentials). Sink: The response.sendError(401, ...) method on line 31. Dataflow: The untrusted message is passed directly into the error response body. Sanitization: None. Because responses generated by sendError are often rendered as HTML by default in many servlet containers, injecting unsanitized exception messages can lead to XSS. Conclusion: Confirmed as a true positive for reflected XSS."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-xss",
