        {
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE:HIGH",
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: multipartFile.getOriginalFilename(). Sink: Path.resolve() call on line 75, used subsequently in Files.copy() on line 77. The application uses the filename provided by the user without sanitizing it for path traversal characters (e.g., '../'). An attacker could potentially upload files to arbitrary locations outside the intended user directory. The dataflow is direct from the multipart request parameter to the file system path resolver. Conclusion: This is a confirmed path traversal vulnerability."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-xss",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: multipartFile.getOriginalFilename(). Sink: Path.resolve() call on line 75, used subsequently in Files.copy() on line 77. The application uses the filename provided by the user without sanitizing it for path traversal characters (e.g., '../'). An attacker could potentially upload files to arbitrary locations outside the intended user directory. The dataflow is direct from the multipart request parameter to the file system path resolver. Conclusion: This is a confirmed path traversal vulnerability."
          },
